 uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District sits at even partisan balance, and first-term Republican Tom Barrett is defending the seat against Democrat William Lawrence in a midterm environment that favors Democrats nationally. Most race raters place the contest between toss-up and lean Democratic, and prediction markets price a Democratic win at roughly 57 to 59 percent. Polling is sparse: the most recent head-to-head, conducted in August by a Democratic firm, showed a two-point Democratic lead.\n\nMoney cuts the other way. Barrett has raised about $6.3 million with $2.9 million on hand, far outpacing Lawrence's $1.1 million, and outside groups have spent against both nominees. A series of debates in early October, along with coverage of Barrett's disagreement with a Trump military action, has kept the race highly visible. The forecast gives Democrats a modest edge, with wide uncertainty given the thin polling record.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}]}